																		&quot;Man of None&quot;
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/identity8866" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5840540); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5840540&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608689319" alt="Identity8866" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5840540)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/identity8866" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5840540); return false;" >Identity8866</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608201524 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Dec 2020 10:38</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4846841">
									

<p>Anyone who acknowledges a relationship between the man and themselves dies painfully within 24 hours.</p>
<p>Seeking Greenlights: Yes, however also seeking advice if possible.</p>
<p>Page Type: SCP Article.</p>
<p>Genre (Optional): Horror / Drama / Emotional</p>
<p>Page Layout (Optional): It'll begin as a standardized SCP document, listing the object class, containment procedures, etc etc. The bulk of the article, however, will be inside of the addendum - the interviews, more specifically.</p>
<p>Elevator Pitch: A man under the affect of a seeming &quot;curse&quot;. Anyone who verbally confirms any relationship between them and the man dies within the next 24 hours in an unspeakably horrific way, varying from person to person.</p>
<p>Central Narrative: <strong>Man of None&quot;</strong>, a concept I had for an SCP, is a seemingly regular man with a personal love for technology. However, what is strange is the fact <em>anyone who verbally recognizes a relationship between the speaker and the object are killed within 24 hours in an unspeakably painful way.</em> While this may seem as if it's simply for the shock factor of gore and horrific deaths, there's a much darker thing behind it.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>He wants to die, however due to the nature of the SCP Foundation his death would be something which would not be wanted. So, they contain him and give him psychological treatment (of course on a very strict regiment), however it never helps. With plenty of research, the only way which suicide patients are helped is via forming relationships with those who help them. And, any relationship with him causes horrific death. <span style="font-size:80%;"><em>So, he's left alone in the world. All that people will call him is an object. They will not say he's their &quot;friend&quot;. Not a &quot;loved one&quot;. &quot;Family&quot;, &quot;enemy&quot;, any of the sort is never heard from them.</em></span></p>
<p>Hook/Attention-Grabber: SCP-XXXX is a person who has a horrifically frail ego and self-esteem, however wants the best for others. He is <em>absolutely</em> desperate for some form of recognition, approval, or relationship between another human. However, due to the nature of his &quot;curse&quot;, he's unable to. This plays to one of the largest human fears of being truly alone. He, at first, tries to isolate himself from other people as to not harm them, however the more he isolates himself the more he becomes desperate to have confirmation in himself and social interaction. And when his greed takes over and he tries to reach out, the people he love die in a horrifically unspeakable way. Watching that is a trauma which most cannot imagine.</p>
<p>Additional Notes: I'm horrific when it comes to formatting first of all, so if I've messed this up please tell me. I'd like criticism on the entire thing really.</p>
</div>
</div>
