<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Identity8866. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>Overall, the concept was interesting at first, especially since you seem to be questioning the nature of human interactions and whether truly “No man is an island”.</p>
<p>Unfortunately, the concept falls apart rapidly due to plot inconsistencies or overcomplications that are not well explained. Why, for example, do people do when this happens? I believe it’s never explained / hinted at throughout your concept. Who placed this curse on him, and why?</p>
<p>Secondly, I don’t understand the nature of the anomaly. Okay, so they die “horrific” deaths, but how and why in those manners? You realise that a “horrific” death can be incredibly subjective, right? Some people would be terrified of dying alone, for example. More importantly, is there a reason <em>why</em> they die in such a manner?</p>
<p>Additionally, the concept itself is vague as “relationship” can mean pretty much anything? You mention “friend”, “enemy” and “loved one”, but isn’t an acquaintance also considered a relationship? Wouldn’t the Foundation agents who try and contain the man also be affected then?</p>
<p>Finally, I don’t understand that whole angle with suicide patients. How are they being “helped”?</p>
<p>Overall, there are too many plot issues for me to understand this fully. If you do decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. Best of luck!</p>

