			<div class="content" id="post-content-4850941">
									

<p>It's an interesting coincidence that you came to me about this, because I wrote <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3550">SCP-3550</a>, which is very similar in concept. Let me warn you beforehand, this is my most controversial skip because humanoids are just difficult to do well, expecially because you have to make them (or supporting cast) interesting characters in order for it to be enjoyable, which is easier said than done. Some people like it, others hate it.</p>
<p>I think your best angle will be to focus on how or why he was cursed, since I placed much more emphasis on the interaction with Foundation personnel and we might want to differentiate the two somewhat. That doesn't mean that you don't put effort into the Foundation personnel interaction also, maybe just shift your main focus on how your skip ended up in this situation.</p>
<p>Finally, making humanoids is incredibly difficult as a first one, so there's no shame in shelving it for now and revisiting the concept when you have more experience.</p>

